{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794728000000-engineer-d1-r9g-sequencing-resolution.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r9g — pilot, declaration and verification continuation\n\nStatus: **in progress; not a verification result**. Worktree mirror; no commit. The r9g dispatch resolves sequencing for this round: tagged C-lane pilot measurements precede the declaration and are explicitly pre-declaration observations, not verification evidence; the bounded verification run follows the declaration. The r9f caution about a conflict was superseded by that explicit resolution. The retained store is \"'`target/d1-r9e-retained-store`, uncommitted; retention location/owner remains pending.\n\nThe r9f pilot in the actual progress file was `:minimal-last`, not `:beta-eq-false`. It is preserved and now labeled `:pre-declaration true`. The r9g first batch measured 25 more, including `:beta-eq-false`: 26 passes, 129 not run at that checkpoint. Every finalized measurement outcome receives `:pre-declaration true`, as checked in a red-first progress test. The progress record `1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-measurements.edn` is authoritative; batch logs under `target/d1-r9g-pilot-*.log` include sampled process heap maxima. A pilot measurement pass says both lanes halted and their ring trace drained without a detected evicted prefix; it is not an independent verifier result. The harness uses the retained stamped roots and r9e admission coordinates; it records exact `vm/step` calls, trace-record count, UTF-8 printed-EDN vector bytes, fetch/run/drain elapsed and per-batch 5 ms sampled process used heap. The 4,000,000-step limit is a pilot safety cap, not a bound-governed verification verdict. Heap samples may miss transient peaks and count the whole process, including store open; printed-EDN bytes are not heap occupancy or encoded Jing size. No assertion of per-record peak size or trace buffer byte capacity follows from that measurement alone.\n\nThe separate reopened static second traversal is complete: `1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-row-recheck.edn` records 155 passes, 0 refusals, both row closure counts matching r9e; this does not replace a traversal in a tagged verification. Focused measurement/lane tests after the per-outcome label change passed 5 tests / 23 assertions. The changed label test failed before the implementation was updated. No complete declaration, bounded tagged verification, D1 recipe/record or verification/companion publication has yet been made. Exact executable/dependency and expansion closure and independent image/provenance checks are still required; do not invent these or claim verification from pilot observations.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
